Done. Usage:

```tsx
// Basic
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary
  fallback={(error, reset) => (
    <div>
      <p>{error.message}</p>
      <button onClick={reset}>Retry</button>
    </div>
  )}
  onError={(error, info) => reportToSentry(error, info)}
>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

Key design decisions:
- `getDerivedStateFromError` captures the error into state (triggers fallback render)
- `componentDidCatch` handles logging — both `console.error` and optional `onError` prop for external reporters (Sentry, etc.)
- `reset` clears error state, re-mounting children on retry
- Custom `fallback` render prop overrides the default UI when you need full control
